{"availability":"available","full":"mutativejs/travels","name":"travels","description":"A fast, framework-agnostic undo/redo core powered by Mutative JSON Patch","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":919,"forks":10,"created":"2025-09-30T08:48:36Z","updated":"2026-08-26T16:33:28Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mutativejs.github.io/travels/","topics":["redo","time-tracking","undo","undo-redo"],"demo":"https://mutativejs.github.io/travels/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:48.647Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:48.647Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:48.647Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T01:08:48.647Z","stars":919,"forks":10}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Patch-based undo/redo optimized for large state, small updates, long history, and persistence.","Travels gives your users the power to undo and redo their actions—essential for text editors, drawing apps, form builders, and any interactive application. Unlike traditional undo systems that copy entire state objects for each change, Travels stores only the differences (JSON Patches), making history much smaller to keep in memory and persist when updates touch a small part of a large state tree.","Works with React, Vue, Zustand, or vanilla JavaScript."],"features":["Why Travels? Performance That Scales","Choosing the Right Undo Strategy","Controlled Journal: Integrate an External State Owner","Mutable Mode: Keep Reactive State In Place","Archive Mode: Control When Changes Are Saved"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mutativejs/travels/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"09a72fd5668f236d360562a59c918fa40f43481d5795ff4f58082ebedb4ca852","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:48.804Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T01:08:48.804Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Patch-based undo/redo optimized for large state, small updates, long history, and persistence.","sourceUrl":"https://gi